WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.968
-It is great to see you, buddy.
-Thank you for having me. Yeah.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:07.167
-Clearly, they know who you are.
-Yeah. Hi.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.367
Welcome to the show.
I'm a fan, as well, by the way.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:12.801
-Hey...

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:17.467
-I heard this backstage, but
this is your talk-show debut?

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.167
-It's my first-ever
talk show, yeah.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.701
-I appreciate it, buddy.
Thank you.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.067
-It's so nice to be here,

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.734
because I very nearly
didn't make it.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:26.868
-What? What do you mean?

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.501
-I was held up
at immigration yesterday.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:32.334
-[ Gasps ] Oh, gosh.
-Ever been secondary?

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.868
Ever been secondary? Anyone?
-No.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.667
-No? Oh, it's not so fun.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.100
I was taken into -- I guess
what you could call it --

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.667
It was more of a dungeon.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.968
And I was asked to wait there
for about 20 minutes.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:48.400
And then I was summoned to this
desk, where someone asked me,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.601
"What are you doing
in the United States, sir?"

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.234
I said, "Well, I'm actually here

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.434
to meet Jimmy Fallon
on 'The Tonight Show.'"

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:57.734
-Yeah.
-And he didn't believe me.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:02.701
And one of his colleagues looked
over at me, looked to him, said,

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:05.000
"Leave Eddie alone."

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.367
And then...
♪♪

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:13.300
And then he said, "Who are you?
I don't know."

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.667
He's like, "It's Eddie from
'Stranger Things.'"

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.601
He's like,
"You're Eddie Munson?"

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.567
And I was like, "Kind of."

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:22.334
He was like,
"Do you come back next season?"

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.000
And I said, "Um, I don't know."

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.400
And he was like, "You better,"
gave me the passport.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.434
-And there you go.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.334
That's the power of
Eddie Munson.

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:33.634
-Crazy. Crazy, crazy.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.267
But I'm very glad
that you let me come,

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.467
because I brought
you a present, Jimmy.

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.234
-You don't have to bring me --
-Well, no, no, no.

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:42.200
But I wanted to.
-What?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.767
-We're missing a member.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.434
-Wow.
-Hey.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.901
-No way.
-Yeah, no, no, no, no, no.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.334
-Really?
-We'd be honored.

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.434
-I am honored.
I am part of the Hellfire Club?

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.100
-Come on.
-Yes!

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.434
Dude...

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:04.000
Come on. I am honored.
I will wear this. I cannot wait.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Thank you so much
for bringing me this gift.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.067
-No, it's our pleasure.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.567
-I'll wear this
through immigration.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.968
It'll be fantastic.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.334
It's probably been a
crazy couple months for you,

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.767
I can imagine, huh?

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:17.601
-It's been pretty weird, yeah.
It's been amazing, though.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.634
I went to Brazil.
I've never been there before.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:20.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:23.367
Aah. You've been.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.234
People are passionate
about your character.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:29.501
People love you. You crushed it.
-Oh, bless you.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.701
-You're so good.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.300
But, I mean,
what are people connecting with

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.467
with your character?

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.767
-I don't know. I think --

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.834
I went to Comic-Con recently,
and it was so moving

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.834
to see how much people
have identified with him.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.300
And I think it's probably
the fact that he's an outsider,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.033
a little bit kind of
on the fringes of society.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.968
And, yeah, I mean, it's just
such -- It's so moving to see

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.534
how much he means to people.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.000
-I know Jack Black gave
you a shout-out the other night.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.434
-I know.
-I know.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.334
-I love that dude.
-He's the best.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.801
-He's the greatest dude.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:03:00.300
-I've, you know, worshiped that
guy since "School of Rock."

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.734
And, yeah,
that was pretty crazy.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:05.734
-But, also, I mean, it's great
to even just hear you talk,

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.934
because I didn't even know
that you're --

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:11.167
that you're not American.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.767
But you're -- Sorry.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.234
They should've told you that
at immigration.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.133
Yeah, yeah. That's the
first thing they tell you.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:19.234
Yeah, you're not --
But you played it so well.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:22.501
And this was my favorite scene,
I would say.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:23.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.567
You're doing "Master of Puppets"
by Metallica,

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.968
and it was just
the greatest thing.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:36.067
Do you know that song
is nearly 40 years old,

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:38.200
and because of you,
it became the number-1 song

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.300
in the country.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.334
-Yeah.
I get no royalties, though.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.968
-Yeah. Ah, you got to work
on that one, yeah.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.400
-Yeah, no, it's awesome.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.601
-Metallica -- they're, like,
the most legendary band

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:49.367
of all time, and you go, like --
Do you get nervous going like,

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:51.100
"I'm going to do
'Master of Puppets'"?

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.300
-It was kind of nerve-racking,

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.868
but it was a weird point
in the pandemic

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.901
where no one had seen
any live music for ages.

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:59.167
And it was me and Gaten.
You've had Gaten on.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.434
-Yeah.
-Come on.

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:02.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. He's the best.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.601
And it was so fun.

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:06.667
I was nervous, but it was
kind of like a rock concert,

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:10.167
and I got to feel like
a rock star for one night,

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:11.234
and that was pretty great.

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:12.300
-Yeah, one night -- that's all
you need.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.334
-That's all I need.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.467
-But it's legendary.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:15.701
It's now legendary.

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.934
And what you did,
even what you did for Metallica

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.467
too, even, like,
you weren't connected.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.167
It was like you'd made
that song number 1.

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:24.000
I go, "Oh, my gosh.
They must have freaked out."

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.667
You've created memes, GIFs,

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:29.100
everything that you can think of
on the Internet.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.634
There's this thing that
I was looking at on TikTok.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:38.701
It's from @Schmoyoho.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.567
Schmoyoho.
-Schmoyoho.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.000
-Schmoyoho.
-Schmoyoho.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.234
-He made a remix of using your
line, "Chrissy, wake up," and --

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.634
It's the funniest thing.
I don't know if you've seen it.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:50.767
Let's just show the video.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.467
This is --
I think it's your voice

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.934
or as they revoiced it and made
it into, like, a song.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.200
Because you're
like, "Chrissy, wake up,"

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.834
and she's about to get
snapped into pieces.

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.534
But, anyways, check this out.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.534
♪ Chrissy, wake up ♪

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:26.501
-Yeah.
-Did you see that?

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:29.067
-I think I probably got about
15 minutes today

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:31.567
where that wasn't
flying around in my head.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:32.968
So it's nice to have it back.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.267
Yeah, I think it's so funny.
Well done, whoever did that.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:38.000
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.133
People also --
they love your relationship

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.701
in the show with Dustin,
with Gaten,

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:42.868
who we love on the show.

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:45.133
-Romantic boy.
-Yeah.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:47.334
He's a special dude, right?
He's just a talented kid.

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:48.567
-You've had him on here.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:49.834
-He told me -- he goes,
"You have to meet --"

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:50.834
He goes like,
"You got to meet Joe."

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.234
-Oh, did he?
-Yeah.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:54.133
So did Joe.
Joe Keery said the same thing.

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:55.934
-Have you had him on here?

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:58.467
-Yes.
-Sorry.

00:05:58.467 --> 00:05:59.834
-They both love you
and they're like,

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.267
"Oh, wait till --
You're gonna love this guy."

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:02.801
They had
the greatest time with you.

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:04.367
-I had the best time with them.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:06.634
I think I was quite nervous
about this dynamic,

00:06:06.634 --> 00:06:10.567
because, I mean, yeah, I think
you guys have seen the show.

00:06:10.567 --> 00:06:12.367
Gaten and Joe's character,

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:14.734
their dynamic is something
that people really, really like.

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:16.501
And I was very conscious,
like, stepping into it

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.901
and being Gaten's side Joe

00:06:18.901 --> 00:06:20.467
and not really
wanting to step --

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:24.100
-Side Joe.
-Yeah, no, his Joe on the side.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.300
And kind of not wanting to step
on anyone's toes,

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.868
but actually became, like,
the thing that --

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:30.100
one of the things that
I most enjoyed about it,

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.200
because me and Joe
would just compare little

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.968
Gaten anecdotes constantly.

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:36.467
-But, I mean,
your American accent,

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:37.767
as I said earlier,
it's great in the show.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.067
I've heard you do --

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:40.767
I heard that you do
a bunch of different accents.

00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.200
-I do some bad accents.
-Yeah.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.634
Well, I was wondering, tonight,
if you can, if we can hear

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.367
one of Eddie's monologues.

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:48.701
We have it
written on cue cards there.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:51.267
But you do it using
different accents.

00:06:51.267 --> 00:06:54.334
So, do Eddie Munson
if he was from

00:06:54.334 --> 00:06:56.567
different parts of the world.

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:59.133
And for those --
I just want to show the wig,

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.634
because it's just so worth it.

00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:02.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:06.033
So, this is --
I love my T-shirt.

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:08.434
Alright, this is Joseph Quinn
performing a scene from

00:07:08.434 --> 00:07:10.434
"Stranger Things"
with different accents.

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:11.801
Whenever you're ready.
-Whenever I'm ready.

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:14.300
-Yes.
-Okay. Is it to this?

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.834
-Yeah, this one. Yep.
-To this guy?

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.000
-Yep.
-Okay. First one.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.968
-Yep.
-Scottish.

00:07:21.968 --> 00:07:23.434
[ Scottish accent ]
We are the freaks.

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:25.434
[ Normal voice ]
Why's he got a lisp?

00:07:25.434 --> 00:07:27.067
-He doesn't have a lisp.
-Wait.

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:28.334
-He's got a lisp.
-No.

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:29.767
-Why not?
-Okay.

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:31.033
-[ Scottish accent ]
We are the freaks,

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:33.801
because we like to play
a fantasy game.

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:36.200
[ Ding ]
-That's a double.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.300
Double points for that.
Alright.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:40.801
-Okay. Liverpool. Okay.
-Liverpool.

00:07:40.801 --> 00:07:42.534
[ Liverpudlian accent ] Boy...

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:48.067
Boy, as long as you're into band
or science or parties...

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.934
[ Ding ]
-That's pretty good.

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:52.367
-[ Normal voice ]
My mom's from Liverpool,

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:54.200
and she sounds exactly
like that.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.501
Australian.

00:07:55.501 --> 00:07:58.567
[ Australian accent ]
Oh, a bloody game where you toss

00:07:58.567 --> 00:08:00.567
bloody balls
into bloody baskets.

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:02.734
[ Ding ]
-Yes. Very good.

00:08:02.734 --> 00:08:04.634
Oh, New York.
-New York.

00:08:04.634 --> 00:08:06.367
[ New York accent ]
New York. Oh!

00:08:06.367 --> 00:08:08.801
It's forced conformity. Oh!

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:12.367
[ Ding ]
Uh...Welsh.

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:14.567
[ Welsh accent ]
That's what's killin' the kids.

00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:15.801
That's the real monster.

00:08:15.801 --> 00:08:17.567
-That's how you do it
right there!

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:22.067
The real monster.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:24.834
Here's Joseph Quinn in
"Stranger Things."

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:26.434
Take a look at this. Yeah!

00:08:26.434 --> 00:08:29.434
-Hear me now.

00:08:29.434 --> 00:08:33.133
There will be
no more retreating...

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:35.934
from "Eddie the Banished."

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:38.167
-Hey, you're really ready
for bat-tle.

00:08:39.234 --> 00:08:41.934
[ Laughs ]

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:45.200
Do you get it?
Bat-tle.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.334
B-A-T.

00:08:48.434 --> 00:08:50.033
No? Alright.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:51.300
I thought I had some good ones.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.467
-Aah!
-What are you doing?

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:56.968
Aah!

00:08:58.334 --> 00:09:00.133
No wedgies! No wedgies!

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:05.701
-Never change, Dustin Henderson.

00:09:05.701 --> 00:09:07.234
Promise me?

00:09:08.801 --> 00:09:12.033
-I wasn't planning on it.

00:09:12.033 --> 00:09:14.534
-Good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:14.534 --> 00:09:17.667
-Come on.
Dude, please come back.

00:09:17.667 --> 00:09:20.167
Please come back.
Joseph Quinn, everybody.

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:21.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:21.634 --> 00:09:24.934
Season 4 of "Stranger Things"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:09:24.934 --> 00:09:27.534
We'll be right back with
a performance from Toro y Moi.

00:09:27.534 --> 00:09:28.634
Stick around, everybody.

